RULES
Keep all existing working functionality. Use the shared flat design tokens and components (no blur, no translucent surfaces). Real behavior only: no fake buttons or fake results. Every change needs loading/empty/error states and edge-case handling. After each section, run the app and verify before moving on.
PRIVACY POLICY & TERMS (in-app, with Login)
URLs (store once in a constants file, nowhere else):
https://docflow.free.je/privacy/
https://docflow.free.je/terms/
Login screen
Under the primary button, centered caption (12-13sp, secondary text color): "By continuing, you agree to our Terms of Service and Privacy Policy." The two names are accent-blue, underlined on press, each with a 48px touch target
Same links on the first-run/onboarding screen, Settings > About ("Privacy Policy", "Terms of Service" rows with chevrons) and on any sign-up or consent screen
Store the accepted version/date locally; if the policy version constant changes, ask for acceptance again on next launch
Opening behavior
Open INSIDE the app, never the external browser app: use the Capacitor Browser plugin (Chrome Custom Tabs on Android, SFSafariViewController on iOS), toolbar tinted to the current theme, with a close button that returns to the exact previous screen with typed Login input preserved
Only these two allow-listed https URLs may open this way; reject anything else
Offline or failed load (no internet, timeout, 404/5xx): do not show a blank page. Show the bundled offline copy of the same document inside a native screen in the shared style, labeled "Offline copy, last updated <date>" with a "Try online version" button
The bundled offline copies must be kept in sync with the published pages (put the version/date in both)
Content check (the pages themselves must match how the app really behaves)
Data stays on the device; no accounts' data or documents are uploaded
Permissions used: camera (scanning), microphone (AI Mic, only while listening), storage/folder access (only folders the user grants)
The one-time language-pack download for translation, and any network use for opening these pages or the link viewer
Note-sharing links (section 4): content is encoded in the link, processed in the browser, and not stored on the server
No analytics or tracking. Pages must be responsive, readable on a phone, and have a dark theme
FIX UI ERRORS FROM THE SCREENSHOTS
A. "Create Document" dialog
Rename to "New document", subtitle "Stored on this device" (remove "(Open in Word UI)"; the phrase "Word UI" must not appear anywhere in the app: use "Edit")
Solid surface (#FFFFFF / #1B1D20), 28px radius, 40% black scrim. Remove the translucent/frosted look
Format selector: Word (.docx), PowerPoint (.pptx), Excel (.xlsx) as three equal-width chips (40px high, icon + short label) that fit without clipping. If a fourth is added, use snap-scroll with a fade edge. No label may be cut off ("Excel (." is a bug)
Title field: 56px high, 16px radius, visible 1px border (#C9CBD0), 2px blue on focus, label "Document title". Validate: illegal characters, max length, duplicate name (auto-number or show an inline error). Leave the title blank = "Untitled"
"Initial content (optional)": label on its own line, never wrapping next to a control. Below it, the text area (min 120px, scrolls, stays above the keyboard) with an AI Mic button inside its bottom-right corner (see 2C). Move "Noise clean" into a switch in the mic's settings; the chip text must be a single line
Footer: "Cancel" (text button) and a filled blue pill "Create" (48px high, single-line label). The dialog must scroll on small screens and with large font scale
An empty body must create an empty document (0 words); never prefill the body with the title
B. Word document screen (view mode)
Top bar: back, title (single line, proper ellipsis), subtitle "Word • 1 page", then Search, Share, Overflow. Remove the mic from the top bar (one AI Mic entry point only, see 2C)
Control row: a segmented control "Print layout | Reading" (36px high, equal widths, selected = blue tint #E8F0FF with blue text and 1px blue border; unselected = surface with readable text, contrast 4.5:1 or better). Delete the "Edit in Word UI" pill. Show the word count as a small caption in the status line or Details, not in this row. Use the blue accent for every selected state (not teal)
Ruler: show only in edit mode or when enabled in the View menu, with real margin/indent markers; hide it in read mode
Page: render a real page sheet (white, A4/Letter aspect ratio, fit to width with 16px side margins, 1px #E3E4E7 border, no blue border). The page shows ONLY document content: remove "Stored on this device" and any app text from inside the page, and show "Page 1 of 1" as a caption outside and under the sheet. Empty page shows the placeholder "Tap Edit to start typing" and fills the viewport
Single edit entry point: the blue "Edit" FAB (pencil icon + label, 56px high, 16px above the bottom bar). Remove the duplicate "Edit (Word UI)" item from the bottom bar
Bottom bar (56px, icons 24px, labels 12sp minimum, contrast 4.5:1): Export PDF, Versions, Notes, AI Mic. Split "Versions / Notes PDF" into separate Versions and Notes items
Keep the title text from repeating three times: file name in the top bar only; the header inside the page appears only if the user added a header
C. AI Mic (one reusable component used in the dialog, the editor and Notes)
Sizes: 48px touch target, 24px icon. States: idle, asking permission, listening (pulsing ring, live waveform, timer, Stop button), processing, error
Dictation inserts text at the caret (editor) or the field (dialog/notes) with live partial text in gray that turns black when final; Undo removes the last dictation in one step
Languages: English, Hindi, Hinglish; selectable in the mic sheet, remembered locally
Recognition runs on-device (Android on-device recognizer or a bundled/downloaded offline model). If the language model is missing, show a one-time download prompt with size. If on-device noise suppression is not actually implemented, do not label it "Noise Clean"; if it is, expose it as a switch in the mic sheet
Permission denied (including "don't ask again"): explain and offer "Open settings"; the microphone indicator shows only while listening; the mic stops when the screen locks or the app is backgrounded
Edge cases: no speech detected, very long dictation, interrupted by a call, another app holding the mic
D. Same class of errors, everywhere
Audit every screen and dialog for: clipped or wrapping chips and labels, text under 12sp, duplicate actions, translucent/blur surfaces, mixed selection colors, plain-text primary buttons, cramped rows, content hidden behind the keyboard or bottom bar
Add a lint rule or test that fails on font sizes below 12sp and on hardcoded colors outside the tokens file
Test at font scale 100%, 130% and 200%, widths 320, 360, 412 and tablet, light and dark mode, and fix every overflow
NOTES (per-document and standalone)
Notes sheet from the document's bottom bar and a standalone Notes list under Manage > Notes
Create, edit, delete, pin, color label, checklist items, timestamps, search; optional anchor to a page or text selection; all stored locally (SQLite)
Actions: Export notes as PDF (title, date, document name), Share as text, Share as file
AI Mic works inside notes
SHARE NOTE WITH LINK (no server, no database)
Each note has "Share with link". The link carries the note itself, so nothing is uploaded or stored on a server.
Link format: https://docflow.free.je/n/#v1.<payload>
Payload = the note (title, body, created date, optional expiry) compressed with deflate and encoded base64url. The part after # is never sent to the server
Options sheet: Access ("Anyone with the link can read", view-only), Password (optional: AES-256-GCM with a PBKDF2-derived key; the password is never put in the link), Expiry (1 day / 7 days / 30 days / Never)
Result sheet: link, Copy, Share (system share sheet), QR code, and the warning "Anyone who has this link can read this note. A link cannot be revoked once it is shared."
Size limit: if the encoded link is over about 6,000 characters, tell the user and offer Share as PDF/file instead; never silently truncate
"My shared links" list (local only): title, date, expiry, with Copy and "Remove from list". Be honest in the UI that removing it from the list does not disable the link
Static viewer page (hosted on docflow.free.je/n/, a single static HTML page, no backend)
Decodes the fragment in the browser, asks for the password if set, checks expiry (best-effort, since it runs in the browser), and shows a clean read-only note with light/dark theme and a "Open in DocFlow" button
Security: render with textContent or a strict sanitizer (never innerHTML with raw content), strict Content-Security-Policy, no third-party scripts, referrer policy no-referrer, noindex; handle malformed or tampered links with a clear "This link is invalid" page
App Links: publish /.well-known/assetlinks.json so the link opens in DocFlow when installed, and offer "Save as note" on import. Validate and sanitize any imported payload before saving it
Documents (PDF/Word) cannot be shared by link without a server. For files, offer the system share sheet and keep it labeled "Share file".
VERIFY
Login on a fresh install: links visible, open in-app, close returns with input preserved; airplane mode shows the offline copy
Reproduce the two original screenshots' screens and confirm every defect above is gone, at 100% and 200% font scale, light and dark
Dictate in English, Hindi and Hinglish; deny the permission; interrupt the recording
Create a note, share by link with and without a password and expiry, open the link on another phone and a desktop browser, tamper with the link, and exceed the size limit
Search the code and UI for "Word UI", unused strings and sub-12sp text, then fix everything and report what was verified
Implement the multi-page preview drawer for the CameraX batch scanning interface, allowing users to view, reorder, or delete captured pages before finalizing the PDF storage.
